# Line endings are an environment assumption, so they get pinned rather than left to
# whatever core.autocrlf each machine happens to have. The repo stores LF; checkouts on
# Windows may render CRLF, and that is fine — what must not happen is CRLF entering the
# repository, because then the same file differs by platform and every gate that reads
# source has to keep guessing.
#
# All four scanning gates already split on /\r?\n/ and would survive either way. This is
# the class fix rather than four instance fixes. 01-VALIDATION-REPORT §13.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary

# Hash-pinned browser provenance inputs (GS-R12 Option A). browser-input.mjs and
# extract-verified-browser.py verify these files' exact bytes (MANIFEST_SHA256 etc.), so
# they are identities, not source: EOL normalisation would change the checked-out bytes on
# every platform and fail CONFIG_FROZEN_IDENTITY. browser-input.json was pinned with CRLF.
# The signed Packages index legitimately ends in a blank line, hence -whitespace.
config/browser-input.json -text -whitespace
config/browser-provenance/** -text -whitespace
